      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I agree that VRChat needs to make options that include people that are unable to use games or watch things due to their epileptic and photosensitive issues. Due to VRChat taking away mods with their anti-cheat this still leaves a large gap of what they were able to give users. Even outside of this seeing non stop stuff can be annoying for any user as there's no way to negate it. \n\nI hope that VRChat is able to fix this issue quickly and effectively.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
      "_id": "6a200dfc7833b15b165281f2",
      "aiGenerated": false,
      "author": {
        "_id": "6a200a1a86d7b8843b8da84a",
        "alias": "Wild strawberry Roadrunner",
        "aliasID": "6a200a1a86d7b8843b8da84e",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny-assets.io/images/2fba0ef99bb543d5acead714fdb13b45.png",
        "created": "2026-06-03T11:03:54.417Z",
        "name": "Astrild",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": "<redacted>"
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "58c62efae9868f3662e9d9a1",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2026-06-03T11:20:28.713Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "deletedAt": null,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "6a13d3e7b94d2b86707854be",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 1
      },
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Being able to turn them off should be a safety setting option. \n\nNot just for those like myself who just find them obnoxious and childish most of the time. Not just for those with low end pcs or standalone headsets who start to lag due to them. But for first and foremost for those with medical conditions. \n\nThey shouldn't be forced to go through a whole instance list to manually turn off everyone's items manually. Let alone they have to keep track of new people joining the instance and turning them off too. I can't imagine how anxious these people must be, despite them trying their best and taking their own responsibility to turn off the items manually. \n\nYou seem to have the technology for it because instance owners can turn them off. Let us do it on a personal base as well.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
    {
      "_id": "6a24a5cffe83f7f1a6c5080f",
      "aiGenerated": false,
      "author": {
        "_id": "62def955df935044abf7586e",
        "alias": "Similar Quail",
        "aliasID": "66312149d36452c1797113ef",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny-assets.io/images/80d7fa4e938c061d62ed2d30aa7cb912.png",
        "created": "2022-07-25T20:13:09.097Z",
        "name": "T e r r a",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": "<redacted>"
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "58c62efae9868f3662e9d9a1",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2026-06-06T22:57:19.019Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "deletedAt": null,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "6a13d3e7b94d2b86707854be",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 2
      },
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "As a creator and someone with a vested interest in VRChat's long term health, as well as just a human being with differently abled friends: I support this 100%.\n\nVRChat is many things, but I think the most prominent feature is that it enables people to gather and create communities of diverse people. This is the image they've built over years, but when accessibility problems like this occur I think it's a very negative detraction from that image. I understand this isn't a profitable thing to ask for, but I think without proper accessibility settings it will alienate individuals and even worse: cause physical harm to certain payers.\n\nBut this isn't even restrictive to photosensitive people, this is a genuine performance setting that would help every user increase their quality of life while playing. VRChat's team has recognized performance as an issue by giving players the ability to customize safety settings, graphical options, and other recent changes. Knowing that this is a focus of VRChat's team, would this not be under that category? Allowing users to disable these settings would be yet another effort for increasing QOL, even if it's only minor for performance it still is a contribution to player choice.\n\nSo in conclusion, for the sake of the differently abled and for those without 5090's, this is a positive change that will have minimal negative effects while increasing accessibility and QOL for players.\n\nTLDR: Accessibility for everyone is important for the VRChat image, and overall performance increasing settings for users is never a bad thing.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-05-25T04:45:27.392Z",
  "deleteID": null,
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "There is currently no option to disable fancy portals.\n\nThere is currently no option to disable join/leave animations.\n\nThere is currently no option to disable items without being world host.\n\nHaving an option in safety settings would mitigate performance dips and be safer for users by giving users control of/ the ability to disable uncontrollable particles/ animations. For epileptic and photosensitive users, disabling items individually is tedious and problematic, some of us can not look at items to disable them without risking medical problems. The same can be said for fancy portals and join/ leave animations if people join/leave near you, we do not have control over placement. \n\nGive us an option to disable these in the safety settings.",
